      "content": "The current presentation of the ablation studies exhibits an insufficient delineation of component efficacy, suggesting a potential oversight in isolating the true marginal gain of the multi-head attention mechanism. The reliance on standard MSE/MAE metrics presents a significant limitation, as these metrics fail to adequately address potential distributional shifts or catastrophic forecasting errors, which remains unclear in the current evaluation framework. Moreover, the comparative analysis lacks sufficient depth; the authors fail to address the inherent computational complexity trade-offs, which constitutes a critical omission in a rigorous assessment of practical applicability.",
      "source": "target",
